problems.problem:
Each cell of an $m\times n$ table ($m$ rows and $n$ columns) contains one of the numbers $1, 50, 100$. Find all possible values of $m$ and $n$ if it is known that the following two conditions hold simultaneously:
(a) for any two rows of the table, the sums of the numbers written in them are equal;
(b) for any two rows of the table, the sums of the squares of the numbers written in them are not equal.

For given positive integers $m>1$ and $n>1$, a coin is placed in each cell of an $m\times n$ table. All coins show tails. Each step consists of the following three operations:
(a) choose a $2\times 2$ square of the table;
(b) turn over the coins in the upper-left and lower-right corners of the chosen square;
(c) turn over one of the coins in the upper-right and lower-left corners of the chosen square.
Find all possible values of the pair $(m,n)$ for which one can perform such steps so that all coins show heads.
